    "8.4 Escribir prueba de propiedad para campos opcionales": {
      "status": "failed",
      "failingExample": "Property 4 (\"Los campos opcionales no afectan la completitud\") FAILED with: Expected 'incomplete' to be 'complete' (spec line 418).\n\nRoot cause (confirmed by isolated repro): ProfileCompletenessService.isPresent treats a JS Date as ABSENT. For an object value it returns `Object.keys(value).length > 0`, and `Object.keys(new Date()).length === 0`. So the required field `common.birthDate` (typed `Date`, Req 5.3) is classified absent even when set, forcing the fallback path to return 'incomplete' for any otherwise-complete profile.\n\nMinimal counterexample profile (all required fields present, birthDate a valid Date):\n{\n  id: 'p-1',\n  common: {\n    profilePhoto: { fileName: 'a', url: 'b' },\n    email: 'e', firstName: 'f', lastName: 'l',\n    birthDate: new Date(),\n    identityDocumentNumber: 'i', documentTypeId: 'd',\n    idCardVerification: { fileName: 'a', url: 'b' },\n    nationalityId: 'n', sexId: 's', personTypeId: 'p'\n  }\n}\nflag: any non-boolean (e.g. null)\n=> resolve() returns { status: 'incomplete', errored: false }, expected 'complete'.\n\nTriage: the test faithfully models Property 4 / Req 5.5 (a set birthDate is present). This is a genuine defect in the resolver's isPresent (Date handling) rather than a test error. Not fixed per PBT workflow — reported for user decision. Note: Property 3 (task 8.3) also uses fc.date() as a \"present\" birthDate value and currently passes, likely because its 200-run search did not hit the all-required-present case; the same defect could surface there.",
